1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,385
A full walkthrough of Thenar, live on Monad testnet.

2
00:00:03,415 --> 00:00:05,160
Every transaction is real.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:09,014
Robots learn from human demonstrations, and the people

4
00:00:09,044 --> 00:00:11,267
who record them are rarely paid and never own the

5
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:13,983
result. Thenar is for them.

6
00:00:14,013 --> 00:00:16,873
The front page times Monad's blocks live.

7
00:00:24,656 --> 00:00:27,796
First, the other side: a robotics lab.

8
00:00:27,826 --> 00:00:30,768
Its budget is a Privy server wallet, under a policy that

9
00:00:30,798 --> 00:00:34,900
allows exactly one action, funding a task on Thenar's contract.

10
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,929
It posts a bounty, Privy signs, and Monad makes it

11
00:00:37,959 --> 00:00:41,469
final. Asked to send money anywhere else, Privy refuses.

12
00:00:41,649 --> 00:00:42,896
That's the lab side done:

13
00:00:42,926 --> 00:00:45,949
a funded task, with no payout key on anyone's laptop.

14
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:50,175
An operator arrives. In production they sign in by email

15
00:00:50,205 --> 00:00:53,204
through Privy; here a test wallet is injected.

16
00:00:53,884 --> 00:00:58,931
Next, a passkey: Face ID, a fingerprint or a PIN.

17
00:00:58,961 --> 00:01:02,725
Its public key goes into PasskeyRegistry, and Monad's

18
00:01:02,755 --> 00:01:06,435
P-256 precompile checks every signature, so a paid run

19
00:01:06,465 --> 00:01:07,997
always comes from a person.

20
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:11,558
The server then admits them to the corpus shares.

21
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,725
Through Mera, the passkey also derives the key a

22
00:01:14,755 --> 00:01:17,141
physical SO-101 obeys.

23
00:01:17,821 --> 00:01:19,846
Now the lab's task at the station.

24
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:23,875
It can be driven by keyboard, by a leader arm over USB,

25
00:01:23,905 --> 00:01:27,892
or in a headset. Here it's WebXR, with Meta's emulator

26
00:01:27,922 --> 00:01:29,830
standing in for a Quest 3S.

27
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:33,220
Squeeze to take the arm; it follows the controller

28
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:34,764
millimetre for millimetre.

29
00:01:34,794 --> 00:01:36,680
The trigger closes the jaws.

30
00:01:36,710 --> 00:01:39,153
Lift, carry, and lower it into the ring.

31
00:01:39,183 --> 00:01:41,404
Every sample is kept for the verifier.

32
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:50,159
In tolerance, scored from the same samples the verifier checks.

33
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:55,417
The page prices gas on the limit, the way Monad charges

34
00:01:55,447 --> 00:01:58,993
it. Submit: the verifier re-scores and signs, and one

35
00:01:59,023 --> 00:02:01,454
transaction records the run and pays.

36
00:02:02,134 --> 00:02:06,699
Executed 1.09 s after the send, and final at 1.21 s, on

37
00:02:06,729 --> 00:02:10,102
Monad testnet, measured in this browser.

38
00:02:10,282 --> 00:02:13,398
Details show the txpool, the receipt, and the block

39
00:02:13,428 --> 00:02:16,114
reaching the finalized tag, hash checked.

40
00:02:16,794 --> 00:02:19,979
The run also issues the operator shares of the corpus.

41
00:02:20,659 --> 00:02:24,276
The corpus page: each episode drawn from the samples its

42
00:02:24,306 --> 00:02:28,060
hash commits to, a Merkle root over the paid set, and

43
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:31,747
two ways to buy: a subscription for every task, or one

44
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:33,550
task over x402.

45
00:02:37,109 --> 00:02:39,925
An AI agent with a wallet and no account asks for the

46
00:02:39,955 --> 00:02:44,001
corpus, gets a 402, and pays one cent of USDC.

47
00:02:44,031 --> 00:02:47,447
Monad's facilitator settles it, and the agent checks the

48
00:02:47,477 --> 00:02:49,675
file against the sale log on chain.

49
00:02:50,355 --> 00:02:52,472
The terms and every sale are public.

50
00:03:02,355 --> 00:03:05,079
Chainlink CRE audits Thenar's server:

51
00:03:05,109 --> 00:03:09,233
it rebuilds each task's Merkle root from the episodes,

52
00:03:09,263 --> 00:03:12,203
reads what's committed on Monad, and writes a verdict to

53
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:17,011
CorpusAudit. This is the CRE simulator, with a real broadcast.

54
00:03:17,691 --> 00:03:20,865
The verdict, uncommitted, sits beside the data for any

55
00:03:20,895 --> 00:03:22,083
buyer to read.

56
00:03:22,763 --> 00:03:25,682
The leaderboard ranks operators by what they've earned,

57
00:03:25,712 --> 00:03:29,281
read back from the trajectory ledger, and agents by what

58
00:03:29,311 --> 00:03:30,313
they've bought.

59
00:03:31,263 --> 00:03:34,693
Finally, the network page reads Monad and Ethereum side

60
00:03:34,723 --> 00:03:39,835
by side: block time, time to final, gas price, and how

61
00:03:39,865 --> 00:03:43,561
each one charges gas. It checks a P-256 signature

62
00:03:43,591 --> 00:03:45,733
through the precompile live.

63
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:48,716
That's Thenar: identity, provenance, payment and

64
00:03:48,746 --> 00:03:51,049
ownership, each enforced on Monad.

